# Installed by deploy/deploy.sh on every deploy (install + daemon-reload).
# Warms the RIS↔ME map of the current GP: ~46 upstream requests that must
# not land on a visitor (docs/ris-join.md §4a). Started by the timer nightly
# and by deploy.sh after each restart, because the Nitro cache is in-memory.
# Since 24.09.2026 the deploy WAITS for this unit instead of firing it with
# --no-block: it is the cold minute after the restart, and a deploy that
# reports success in the middle of it hands that minute to the first visitor.
#
# Second call since 2026-09-17: the homepage now also states what is in
# Begutachtung WITHOUT a Gegenstand at Parliament (docs/architecture.md
# §12.16). It reads the same corpus the first call warms, so it adds no
# upstream traffic — but it has its own 30-minute derived cache, and that
# section is a correction to a claim the page makes, so it must not be the
# one part of the start page that arrives cold. (Its path followed the
# rename to /api/ris-drafts on 2026-09-18 — §12.19.)
#
# Third call since 2026-09-18: the station map behind the station filter
# (§12.26). This is the expensive one — 227 upstream requests for GP XXVIII,
# 650 for XXVII, 35.6 s cold — and the only one that MUST run here: the list
# reads the map under a 2.5 s budget and simply answers without stations when
# it is cold, so a map nobody warms is a filter nobody sees. --max-time 900
# rather than 600 because the timer may fire on a period twice that size.
#
# Fourth call since 2026-09-19: the Bundesgesetzblatt Teil II volumes the
# Verordnung pages read their Kundmachung from (§12.32). Three volumes are
# about 21 requests to RIS when cold — and unlike the other sections, the
# result of a cold run would not merely be slow but a statement: whoever does
# not have the volumes finds no Kundmachung and would write „nicht
# kundgemacht" under a Verordnung that has been in force for a long time.
#
# It stands BEFORE the list call, ever since the list shows the outcome per
# row (§12.32): the list waits only 3 s for it and otherwise renders without
# the column — which is right, but avoidable when the volumes are already in.
#
# Fifth call since 2026-09-26: the station map of the PREVIOUS period. Same
# argument as the fourth call, one period back — the list reads the map under
# a 2,5 s budget, so whoever picks GP XXVII from the period chooser on a cold
# server waits those 2,5 s and then gets a list without the station filter
# plus a note. The note is honest and the filter is the accountability layer,
# so it is the one that must not be missing: the finished period is where the
# question „was ist daraus geworden" has an answer at all.
#
# It is the expensive line — 650 upstream requests against 227 for the
# running period, 35,6 s cold (§12.26) — and it stands LAST because of it:
# every call before it serves a page somebody reaches without choosing
# anything, and a deploy that breaks off in the middle of this unit should
# lose the least-visited warm-up, not the start page's.
#
# `vorperiode` and not `XXVII`, for the reason `aktuell` exists
# (`server/utils/http/params.ts`): a Roman numeral in a unit file is a line
# that goes wrong on exactly the day nobody is watching it, the
# Periodenwechsel — and then it would warm the period that just ended while
# the list shows the one that just began.
#
# MEASURED AND DELIBERATELY NOT DONE: warming
# `/api/drafts/:gp/:inr/konsolidiert` for the drafts in Begutachtung (cold
# ~12 s, warm 10 ms, day cache). Three reasons, and the first is the one that
# decides. That section is the ONLY one on the page that is fetched lazily
# and client-side (`compare/TextComparisonSection.vue`,
# `server: false, lazy: true`): the page renders and reads without it and
# then fills in — nobody is told something false in the meantime, which is
# what separates it from the station map and the BGBl volumes above. Second,
# it is per draft and unbounded: 19 drafts were open on 26.09.2026, so a good
# four minutes added to a deploy this unit blocks by design, and it grows
# with the ME count — a deploy that gets slower every month is a deploy that
# stops being run. Third, each draft pulls every § of every law it amends
# from RIS, nightly, for a layer that is opened on a median 12 % of a draft's
# §§ (§12.12a). The first visitor of the day pays 12 s for a section that
# says „lädt"; that is the right one to pay it.
[Unit]
Description=Begutachtungs-Monitor: warm the RIS corpus, BGBl volumes and both station maps
After=begutachtungs-monitor.service
Requires=begutachtungs-monitor.service
# Since 30.09.2026: the pages of the open drafts, in their own unit and
# without blocking (begutachtungs-monitor-prewarm-pages.service) — after the
# corpora below, which those pages read. OnSuccess= rather than an
# ExecStartPost that runs `systemctl start`: this unit runs as `app`, which
# may not start units, and `ExecStartPost=+…` would hand a root command to an
# otherwise unprivileged job. OnSuccess= queues the job from systemd itself,
# only when every ExecStart below succeeded — the condition ExecStartPost had —
# and without blocking whoever started this unit (deploy.sh, the watchdog).
OnSuccess=begutachtungs-monitor-prewarm-pages.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
# Nothing here needs root: curl against localhost.
User=app
Group=app
NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
# The unit's own worst case, stated rather than inherited: the five --max-time
# budgets below add up to 2.820 s, and deploy.sh blocks on this job.
TimeoutStartSec=2900
# The first request waits for the port. `After=` orders this job behind the
# app's START, not behind its LISTEN: after a hand-typed `systemctl restart`
# the curl came at 16:56:15 and Node listened at 16:56:16 (29.09.2026,
# status 7). deploy.sh only escaped it through its `sleep 2`. Ten seconds of
# connection-refused retries cost nothing when the port is already open.
ExecStart=/usr/bin/curl -fsS -o /dev/null --retry 10 --retry-connrefused --retry-delay 1 --max-time 600 http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/ris-map/aktuell
ExecStart=/usr/bin/curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 300 http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/bgbl/teil2
ExecStart=/usr/bin/curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 120 "http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/ris-drafts?status=open"
ExecStart=/usr/bin/curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 900 http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/stations/aktuell
ExecStart=/usr/bin/curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 900 http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/stations/vorperiode
